NOTE ON BUNDLED AND INVOKED THIRD-PARTY CODE

ComboBatch is an MIT-licensed wrapper. It invokes, and in one case vendors,
third-party software under its own licence terms:

  * The vendored Shambhala2 implementation under combobatch/vendor/shambhala/
    carries its upstream licence; see the LICENSE file in that directory.
  * The R packages installed into the Docker image (limma, sva, edgeR, DESeq2,
    bapred, and others) are licensed individually, several under the GPL.
    ComboBatch calls them through rpy2 rather than distributing them, and the
    image is a convenience build, not a redistribution of their source.
  * The example dataset under examples/example_dataset/ is derived from public
    GEO series; per-series attribution is in that directory's PROVENANCE.md.


